Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:32:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Size the molecule editor before its window is created

Qt creates the native window of a dialog when it is shown, before the dialog
is sized, so the window starts at the default 100x30. With --stereo the
viewer draws into that window and the first frame it commits is 100x30;
under Wayland the compositor takes the window's size from the intersection
of the window geometry and the surface, and shrinks the dialog to that frame.
Sizing the dialog when it is built creates the window at its own size.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
 src/tools/moleculeview.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp b/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp
index 1888d829..242c60a3 100644
--- a/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp
+++ b/src/tools/moleculeview.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,10 @@ MoleculeDialog::MoleculeDialog(QWidget *parent)
             break;
         }
     }
+
+    // Qt creates the window of a dialog before it sizes it. The viewer draws into that window,
+    // and a first frame at the unsized default would make the compositor shrink the dialog to it.
+    adjustSize();
 }
 
 void MoleculeDialog::slotLoadMolecule()
